<problem>
<!--<title>Tangent line to alpha function</title>
<variantControl nVariants='1' /> -->
<setup>

<function name="g" variables="n t" simplify="full" symbolic="true">t^n*e^(1-t)</function>
<function name="g1" variables="t">$$g(1, t)</function>

<function name="gprime" variables="n t" simplify="full" symbolic="true">e^(1 - t) (n - t) t^(-1 + n)</function>
<function name="g1prime" variables="t" simplify="full">e^(1-t) (1-t)</function>
<math name="L10" simplify="numbers">$$g1(0)+$$g1prime(0)*(t-0)</math>
<math name="L11" simplify="numbers">$$g1(1)+$$g1prime(1)*(t-1)</math>
<number name="g10">$$g1(0)</number>
<number name="g11">$$g1(1)</number>
<number name="g1prime0">$$g1prime(0)</number>
<number name="g1prime1">$$g1prime(1)</number>
<number name="one">1</number>
<number name="two">2</number>
<number name="zero">0</number>
<number name="three">3</number>


<function name="g2" variables="t">$$g(2, t)</function>
<function name="g2prime" variables="t">$$gprime(2, t)</function>
<math name="L20" simplify="numbers">$$g(2, 0)+$$g2prime(0)*(t-0)</math>
<math name="L21" simplify="numbers">$$g(2, 1)+$$g2prime(1)*(t-1)</math>
<math name="L22" simplify="numbers">$$g(2, 2)+$$g2prime(2)*(t-2)</math>
<number name="g20">$$g(2, 0)</number>
<number name="g2prime0">$$g2prime(0)</number>
<number name="g21">$$g(2, 1)</number>
<number name="g2prime1">$$g2prime(1)</number>
<number name="g22">$$g(2, 2)</number>
<number name="g2prime2">$$g2prime(2)</number>
<math name="p20">(0,$g20 )</math>
<math name="p21">(1,$g21 )</math>
<math name="p22">(2,$g22 )</math>
<math name="p10">(0,$g10 )</math>
<math name="p11">(1,$g11 )</math>

</setup>

We can find linear approximations of functions of different variables than <m>x</m>.  For example, let <m>g(t)=t^n e^{1-t}</m>, where <m>n</m> is some number.


<exercise>
<p>Let <m>n=1</m>, so <m>g(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award>$g1 </award>
</answer>
 and <m>g'(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award>$g1prime </award>
</answer>
</p>

<p>Find the equation for the tangent line of <m>g</m> at <m>t=0</m>.
</p>
<p>

<m>y=</m> 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$L10 </award>
</answer>
</p>

  
<p>Find the equation for the linear approximation of <m>g</m> around <m>t=1</m>
</p>
<p>

<m>L_{1}(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$L11 </award>
</answer>
</p>

  <hint>
Linear approximation and tangent line are the same thing.  You should repeat the same calculations, once for <m>t=0</m> and once from <m>t=1</m>.

</hint>

<p>On the below graph of <m>g</m>, plot the tangent lines corresponding to these two linear approximations.</p>



<math hide="true" name="px1">3</math>
<math hide="true" name="px2">0.5</math>


<graph size="medium" aspectRatio="5/3" xmin="-2" xmax="7" ymin="-1" ymax="4" showNavigation="false">

<function extend="$g1" />

<point hide="true" name="snap1">(0, $$g1(0))</point>
<point hide="true" name="snap2">(1, $$g1(1))</point>

<point stylenumber="2" name="tangentAnchor1" x="$px1" y="$$g1($px1 )">

  <attractTo>$snap1</attractTo>
  <attractTo>$snap2</attractTo>
  <constrainToGraph />

</point>
<line draggable="false" stylenumber="2" through="$tangentAnchor1" slope="$$g1prime($tangentAnchor1.x )" />

<point stylenumber="2" name="tangentAnchor2" x="$px2" y="$$g1($px2 )">

  <attractTo>$snap1</attractTo>
  <attractTo>$snap2</attractTo>
  <constrainToGraph />

</point>
<line draggable="false" stylenumber="2" through="$tangentAnchor2" slope="$$g1prime($tangentAnchor2.x )" />


</graph>

<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true"><when>($px1, $px2) = (0, 1)</when></award>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise>
Let <m>n=2</m>, so <m>g(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award>$g2 </award>
</answer>
 and <m>g'(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award>$g2prime </award>
</answer>


<p>Find the equation for the tangent line of <m>g</m> at <m>t=0</m>.
</p>
<p>

<m>y=</m> 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$L20 </award>
<award credit="0.5" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L20 </award>
<award credit="0.25" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L20 </award>
</answer>
<copy prop="feedbacks" source="answer7" />
</p>

<p>Find the equation for the linear approximation of <m>g</m> around <m>t=1</m>
</p>
<p>

<m>L_{1}(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$L21 </award>
<award credit="0.5" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L21 </award>
<award credit="0.25" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L21 </award>
</answer>
<copy prop="feedbacks" source="answer8" />
</p>

<p>Find the equation for the linear approximation of <m>g</m> around <m>t=2</m>
</p>
<p>

<m>L_{2}(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$L22 </award>
<award credit="0.5" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L22 </award>
<award credit="0.25" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$L22 </award>
</answer>
<copy prop="feedbacks" source="answer9" />
</p>

<p>On the below graph of <m>g</m>, plot the tangent lines corresponding to these three linear approximations.</p>


<!-- django tag applet, alpha_function_tangents, width=500, height=300, n=2, answer_n_t=three answer_x1=zero answer_x2=one answer_x3=two answer_n=two -->

<math hide="true" name="px3">3</math>
<math hide="true" name="px4">0.5</math>
<math hide="true" name="px5">6</math>

<graph size="medium" aspectRatio="5/3" xmin="-2" xmax="7" ymin="-1" ymax="4" showNavigation="false">

<function extend="$g2" />

<point hide="true" name="snap3">(0, $$g2(0))</point>
<point hide="true" name="snap4">(1, $$g2(1))</point>
<point hide="true" name="snap5">(2, $$g2(2))</point>


<point stylenumber="2" name="tangentAnchor3" x="$px3" y="$$g2($px3 )">

<attractTo>$snap3</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap4</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap5</attractTo>
<constrainToGraph />

</point>
<line draggable="false" stylenumber="2" through="$tangentAnchor3" slope="$$g2prime($tangentAnchor3.x )" />


<point stylenumber="2" name="tangentAnchor4" x="$px4" y="$$g2($px4 )">

<attractTo>$snap3</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap4</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap5</attractTo>
<constrainToGraph />

</point>
<line draggable="false" stylenumber="2" through="$tangentAnchor4" slope="$$g2prime($tangentAnchor4.x )" />


<point stylenumber="2" name="tangentAnchor5" x="$px5" y="$$g2($px5 )">

<attractTo>$snap3</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap4</attractTo>
<attractTo>$snap5</attractTo>
<constrainToGraph />

</point>
<line draggable="false" stylenumber="2" through="$tangentAnchor5" slope="$$g2prime($tangentAnchor5.x )" />


</graph>

<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true"><when>
($px3, $px4, $px5) = (0, 1, 2)
</when></award>
</answer>
</exercise>


<solution>

<exercise>
<p><m>g(t)= $g1</m>, <m>g'(t) = $g1prime </m>.</p>

<p><m>t=0</m>:  <m>g(0)=$g10 </m>, <m>g'(0)=$g1prime0 </m>, <m>y=et \approx <round numDigits="4">e</round>t</m>.</p>

<p><m>t=1</m>: <m>g(1)= $g11 </m>, <m>g'(1)=$g1prime1 </m>, <m>L(t)=<round numDigits="4"><number>$L11 </number></round></m></p>


<graph size="medium" aspectRatio="5/3" xmin="-2" xmax="7" ymin="-1" ymax="4" showNavigation="false">

<function extend="$g1" />
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true" name="p1">(0, $$g1(0))</point>
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true" name="p2">(1, $$g1(1))</point>
<line stylenumber="2" fixed="true" through="$p1" slope="$$g1prime(0)" />
<line stylenumber="2" fixed="true" through="$p2" slope="$$g1prime(1)" />

</graph>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p><m>g(t)=t^2e^{1-t}</m>. <m>g'(t)=(2t-t^2)e^{1-t} = t(2-t)e^{1-t}</m>.</p>

<p><m>t=0</m>: <m>g(0)=$g20 </m>, <m>g'(0)=$g2prime0 </m>, <m>y= $L20</m>.</p>

<p><m>t=1</m>:  <m>g(1)=$g21 </m>, <m>g'(1)=$g2prime1 </m>, <m>L_{1}(t)=1(t-1)+1 = $L21</m></p>

<p><m>t=2</m>:  <m>g(2)=<evaluate function="$g2" input="2" forceSymbolic="true" simplify="true" name="g22s" /> </m>, <m>f'(2)=$g2prime2</m>, <m>L_{2}(t)=$g22s  \approx <round numDigits="4"><number>$L22 </number></round></m>.

</p>

<graph size="medium" aspectRatio="5/3" xmin="-2" xmax="7" ymin="-1" ymax="4" showNavigation="false">

<function extend="$g2" />
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true" name="p3">(0, $$g2(0))</point>
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true" name="p4">(1, $$g2(1))</point>
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true" name="p5">(2, $$g2(2))</point>
<line stylenumber="2" fixed="true" through="$p3" slope="$$g2prime(0)" />
<line stylenumber="2" fixed="true" through="$p4" slope="$$g2prime(1)" />
<line stylenumber="2" fixed="true" through="$p5" slope="$$g2prime(2)" />

</graph>
</exercise>


</solution>


</problem>